    "recommendations": "• Mark the single access point with a clearly visible address sign readable from the access road in both directions of approach.\n\n• Post a site map at the access point showing the locations of all three structures, the internal drive aisle, and the dumpster enclosure.\n\n• Mark each structure with a distinct identifier (e.g., Building A, Building B, Building C) visible from the internal drive aisle.\n\n• Keep the internal drive aisle clear of parked vehicles to allow emergency vehicles to reach all three structures.\n\n• Identify and mark the closest point of vehicle access to the rear of each structure, as rear access is limited.\n\n• Keep the area around the dumpster enclosure clear so it does not block emergency vehicle movement along the drive aisle.\n\n• Trim vegetation along the access road and internal drive aisle to maintain sight lines and overhead clearance for emergency vehicles.\n\n• Identify a designated staging area within the property that emergency vehicles can use without blocking the single access point.\n\n• Mark any dead-end sections of the internal drive aisle so responders know where turnaround space is available."
